```python
def extended_gcd(a, b):
    if b == 0:
        return (a, 1, 0)
    g, x, y = extended_gcd(b, a % b)
    return (g, y, x - (a // b) * y)
```

This is the same back-substitution as the Lean definition `xgcd`, whose correctness (`bezout`) is proved for all inputs. On $(1071, 462)$ it returns $(21, -3, 7)$: $1071 \cdot (-3) + 462 \cdot 7 = 21$.
